time=2026-10-16T23:46:19.445Z level=INFO msg="model prompt" record=prov-2026-75646f74 attempt=1 prompt="## The change\n\nThe provenance clone command (blueprint prov-2026-fe19dbf4, section 5), in two files.\n\nWiring, cmd/provenance/clone_cmd.go (cobra package): a top-level command, use \"clone DIR [id...]\", short \"Create a local project from your published records\", arity min_one. No flags.\n\nBehaviour is fixed by cmd/provenance/clone_test.go: needs a session; DIR must be absent or empty; writes the record files, every version snapshot, .provenance.yml, the manifest and .gitattributes; does not run git.\n\nLogic, cmd/provenance/clone_run.go:\n\nFile cmd/provenance/clone_run.go (go package, package main). Imports, each its own addImport, exactly these: fmt, io, os, path/filepath, github.com/spf13/cobra, github.com/livecodelife/provenance/record, github.com/livecodelife/provenance/remote.\n\nDeclarations, in this order, each exactly one set* call (file kwarg cmd/provenance/clone_run.go) whose code kwarg is the code below verbatim (gofmt-formatted, comments kept). Do not alter, reorder or add anything. A const or var group is one setConst or setVar named after its first name; setMethod takes receiver and name separately.\n\n  - setFunction name runClone, code exactly:\n      func runClone(out io.Writer, cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {\n      \tdir, ids := args[0], args[1:]\n      \tif entries, err := os.ReadDir(dir); err == nil && len(entries) > 0 {\n      \t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%s is not empty\", dir)\n      \t}\n      \tclient, err := apiClient()\n      \tif err != nil {\n      \t\treturn err\n      \t}\n      \troot, err := filepath.Abs(dir)\n      \tif err != nil {\n      \t\treturn err\n      \t}\n      \tif err := os.MkdirAll(root, 0o755); err != nil {\n      \t\treturn err\n      \t}\n      \tstore := &record.FilesStore{Root: root, Dir: \"provenance\"}\n      \tn, err := remote.CloneRecords(cmd.Context(), client, store, ids)\n      \tif err != nil {\n      \t\treturn err\n      \t}\n      \tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(root, configFile), []byte(initConfig), 0o644); err != nil {\n      \t\treturn err\n      \t}\n      \tlines, err := record.BuildManifest(store)\n      \tif err != nil {\n      \t\treturn err\n      \t}\n      \tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Join(root, filepath.Dir(manifestPath)), 0o755); err != nil {\n      \t\treturn err\n      \t}\n      \tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(root, manifestPath), record.MarshalManifest(lines), 0o644); err != nil {\n      \t\treturn err\n      \t}\n      \tif _, err := ensureGitattributes(root, \"provenance\"); err != nil {\n      \t\treturn err\n      \t}\n      \tfmt.Fprintf(out, \"\\n✓ Cloned %d record(s) into %s\\n  Every version was verified against its content hash.\\n  Spec files are not published: lint reports them until the repository's files are present.\\n  Run git init and commit when you are ready.\\n\\n\", n, dir)\n      \treturn nil\n      }\n\n## Supplementary context\n\nThis section is supplied by the caller, not by the record. It is advisory: it does not add to or change what the record authorized, and the files below remain the only ones the actions may reach.\n\nCaller notes:\n\n# Context for sedum grow (the cmd/provenance CLI and the record package)\n\nPass with: sedum-haiku grow --generators generators --records provenance --prompt-file .sedum/context.md --only <id>\nAdvisory only: behaviour belongs in the record. Editing this file does not regenerate anything.\n\nConventions: cmd/provenance (package main)\n- Package main, cmd/provenance. Every run function is func run<Cmd>(out io.Writer, cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error and prints through out, never os.Stdout. User-facing errors go through r.fail(format, args...), then return an error.\n- Each import is its own addImport. Write exactly `_, skip := ...` when a binding would otherwise be unused.\n- Generated Go is gofmt-clean and calls only helpers listed here or in the record.\n\nHelpers that exist in package main (call, do not redefine)\n- openRepo(cmd *cobra.Command) (*repo, error); repo has Root string, Config config, Store *record.FilesStore.\n- (r *repo) resolve(id string) (*record.Record, *record.Document, error) prints its own message.\n- (r *repo) recordPath(id) string and versionsDir(id) string (relative to r.Root); const manifestPath; (r *repo) writeManifest() error; author() string; fail(format string, args ...any).\n- (r *repo) git(args ...string) (string, error); commit(message string, paths ...string) error; unstage(paths ...string).\n- snapshotFiles(paths ...string) []fileState; restoreFiles(states []fileState); tag(id string, version int) string gives \"[<id>@<version>]\".\n- recordArg(cmd, args) (string, error) takes the id from --record or the first argument.\n\nRecord library (github.com/livecodelife/provenance/record)\n- Record fields ID, Schema, Status, Version, Title, Intent, Constraints, AffectedScope, ForbiddenScope, Reason, ReasonKind, SealedAtSHA, AssociatedSpecs, Implements, ImplementsVersion.\n- (*Record).ContentHash(specs SpecResolver) (string, []string); (*FilesStore).Specs(), .Versions(id), .Snapshot(id, v), .Save(r, doc), .Load(id), .List().\n- record.Commit(s Store, r *Record, doc *Document, b Bump{Reason, ReasonKind, Author string}) (*Snapshot, error).\n\nConventions: record package\n- Package record (module github.com/livecodelife/provenance). Generated Go is gofmt-clean and calls only helpers listed here or in the record.\n- Canonical encoding is docs/HASHING.md section 5: bytes are written to a *bytes.Buffer; no encoding/json.\n- Each import is its own addImport. Write exactly `_, skip := ...` when a binding would otherwise be unused.\n\nHelpers that exist in package record (call, do not redefine)\n- writeCanonical(b *bytes.Buffer, v any): the encoder switch in hash.go. Its default case panics \"record: non-canonical value type\".\n- writeString(b *bytes.Buffer, s string): a JSON string with only the section 5 escapes.\n- Canonical(v any) string; hashBytes(data []byte) string.\n\nSelections made for this change on an earlier run (context only; they are not applied):\n\n- {\"action\":\"setArgs\",\"kwargs\":{\"arity\":\"min_one\",\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"clone\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/clone_run.go\",\"path\":\"fmt\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/clone_run.go\",\"path\":\"io\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/clone_run.go\",\"path\":\"os\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/clone_run.go\",\"path\":\"path/filepath\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/clone_run.go\",\"path\":\"github.com/spf13/cobra\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/clone_run.go\",\"path\":\"github.com/livecodelife/provenance/record\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"addImport\",\"kwargs\":{\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/clone_run.go\",\"path\":\"github.com/livecodelife/provenance/remote\"}}\n- {\"action\":\"setFunction\",\"kwargs\":{\"code\":\"func runClone(out io.Writer, cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {\\n\\tdir, ids := args[0], args[1:]\\n\\tif entries, err := os.ReadDir(dir); err == nil \\u0026\\u0026 len(entries) \\u003e 0 {\\n\\t\\treturn fmt.Errorf(\\\"%s is not empty\\\", dir)\\n\\t}\\n\\tclient, err := apiClient()\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\troot, err := filepath.Abs(dir)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif err := os.MkdirAll(root, 0o755); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tstore := \\u0026record.FilesStore{Root: root, Dir: \\\"provenance\\\"}\\n\\tn, err := remote.CloneRecords(cmd.Context(), client, store, ids)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(root, configFile), []byte(initConfig), 0o644); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tlines, err := record.BuildManifest(store)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Join(root, filepath.Dir(manifestPath)), 0o755); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(root, manifestPath), record.MarshalManifest(lines), 0o644); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif _, err := ensureGitattributes(root, \\\"provenance\\\"); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tfmt.Fprintf(out, \\\"\\\\n✓ Cloned %d record(s) into %s\\\\n  Every version was verified against its content hash.\\\\n  Run git init and commit when you are ready.\\\\n\\\\n\\\", n, dir)\\n\\treturn nil\\n}\",\"file\":\"cmd/provenance/clone_run.go\",\"name\":\"runClone\"}}\n\n## Already present\n\nThese regions already exist in the files below and belong to other changes. Do not select them: an action that resolves to one of them would conflict with the change that owns it.\n\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: describeRoot {\"bin\":\"provenance\"} (owned by prov-2026-76a125e6; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: addShortPersistentFlag:string {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"flag\":\"config\"} (owned by prov-2026-76a125e6; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"check\"} (owned by prov-2026-063f1395; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"status\"} (owned by prov-2026-12b1ca97; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"deprecate\"} (owned by prov-2026-35439261; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"complete\"} (owned by prov-2026-41fb548c; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"create\"} (owned by prov-2026-44a07768; do not select)\n- cmd/provenance/main.go: registerCommand {\"bin\":\"provenance\",\"command\":\"edit\"} (owned by prov-2026-57b8a95b; do not select)\